#ifndef STATS_H
#define STATS_H

double mean(const int* values, int count);

#endif
```
`stats.cpp`:
```cpp
#include "stats.h"

double mean(const int* values, int count) {
    int total = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < count; ++i) total += values[i];
    return static_cast<double>(total) / count;
}
```
`main.cpp`:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include "stats.h"

int main() {
    int fills[4] = {101, 103, 99, 105};
    std::cout << mean(fills, 4) << '\n';
    return 0;
}
```
Build: `g++ -std=c++17 -c stats.cpp` then `g++ -std=c++17 -c main.cpp` then `g++ -std=c++17 main.o stats.o -o fills`. Output: `102` (since $101+103+99+105 = 408$ and $408/4 = 102$). `echo $?` prints `0` because `main` returned success.
